<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="Is This Real? helps people learn how to spot signs of AI-generated images.">
  <title>Is This Real? | AI Media Awareness</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>

<body>

<header class="site-header">
  <div class="container nav">
    <a class="logo" href="#top">Is This Real?</a>

    <nav>
      <a href="#analyzer">Analyzer</a>
      <a href="#guide">Guide</a>
      <a href="#about">About</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<main id="top">

<section class="hero container">

  <div class="hero-copy">
    <span class="eyebrow">AI MEDIA AWARENESS</span>

    <h1>
      Before you believe it,
      <span>take a closer look.</span>
    </h1>

    <p>
      AI-generated photos are becoming harder to recognize.
      Upload an image to explore common warning signs and learn
      how to check media for yourself.
    </p>

    <a class="primary-button" href="#analyzer">
      Try the analyzer ↓
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="hero-card">
    <div class="scan-line"></div>

    <div class="fake-photo">
      <div class="sun"></div>
      <div class="mountain mountain-one"></div>
      <div class="mountain mountain-two"></div>
      <div class="ground"></div>
      <div class="person"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="scan-label">
      <span></span> VISUAL CHECK
    </div>
  </div>

</section>


<section class="analyzer-section" id="analyzer">

  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">STEP 01</span>

      <h2>Check an image</h2>

      <p>
        Upload a photo to see an educational analysis of visual clues
        that can sometimes appear in AI-generated media.
      </p>
    </div>


    <div class="analyzer-card">

      <label class="drop-zone" id="dropZone">

        <input id="imageInput" type="file" accept="image/*">

        <div class="upload-icon">↑</div>

        <h3>Choose an image</h3>

        <p>
          Upload a photo from your device
        </p>

        <small>
          JPG, PNG or WEBP • Up to 10 MB
        </small>

      </label>


      <div class="preview-area hidden" id="previewArea">

        <div class="preview-wrap">

          <img id="previewImage" alt="Selected image preview">

          <button
            class="remove-button"
            id="removeButton"
            type="button">
            Remove
          </button>

        </div>


        <div class="analysis-controls">

          <p id="fileName"></p>

          <button
            class="primary-button"
            id="analyzeButton"
            type="button">
            Analyze image
          </button>

        </div>

      </div>


      <div class="loading hidden" id="loading">

        <div class="spinner"></div>

        <h3>Examining visual clues...</h3>

        <p>
          Checking the image for common AI-media warning signs.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="result hidden" id="result">

        <div class="result-top">

          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">DEMO ANALYSIS</span>

            <h3 id="resultTitle">
              Analysis complete
            </h3>
          </div>

          <div class="score" id="score">
            --%
          </div>

        </div>


        <div class="meter">
          <div id="meterFill"></div>
        </div>


        <p
          id="resultSummary"
          class="result-summary">
        </p>


        <div
          class="clue-grid"
          id="clueGrid">
        </div>


        <div class="notice">

          <strong>Important:</strong>

          This prototype is an educational demonstration,
          not proof that an image is real or AI-generated.
          Reliable detection requires specialized models,
          provenance information and human judgment.

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

</section>


<section class="guide-section" id="guide">

  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-heading">

      <span class="eyebrow">STEP 02</span>

      <h2>Learn what to look for</h2>

      <p>
        You don't need special software to slow down and
        question a suspicious image.
      </p>

    </div>


    <div class="guide-grid">

      <article class="guide-card">

        <span class="number">01</span>

        <h3>Zoom in</h3>

        <p>
          Look closely at hands, teeth, jewelry, glasses,
          hair and small background details.
        </p>

      </article>


      <article class="guide-card">

        <span class="number">02</span>

        <h3>Read the text</h3>

        <p>
          AI images can contain distorted letters,
          signs, logos or words that don't quite make sense.
        </p>

      </article>


      <article class="guide-card">

        <span class="number">03</span>

        <h3>Check the lighting</h3>

        <p>
          Look for shadows and reflections that don't agree
          with the apparent position of the light source.
        </p>

      </article>


      <article class="guide-card">

        <span class="number">04</span>

        <h3>Verify the source</h3>

        <p>
          Ask who posted it, where it came from and whether
          trustworthy sources show the same event.
        </p>

      </article>

    </div>

  </div>

</section>


<section class="about-section" id="about">

  <div class="container about-card">

    <div>

      <span class="eyebrow">
        WHY THIS EXISTS
      </span>

      <h2>
        AI literacy should be accessible to everyone.
      </h2>

    </div>


    <p>
      Is This Real? is a student-built concept focused on
      helping people—especially those who may be less familiar
      with generative AI—pause, inspect and verify digital
      media before sharing it.
    </p>

  </div>

</section>

</main>


<footer>

  <div class="container footer-inner">

    <span>
      Is This Real? © 2026
    </span>

    <span>
      Built for digital media awareness.
    </span>

  </div>

</footer>


<script src="script.js"></script>

</body>
</html>
